A||||3||Avery Montembeault||help - need info||||1||
Z||000000||Avery Montembeault||02-06-2001||12:14 PM||||I reccently aquired a free 88 fiero. Its in incredible shape, but the 4 cylinder engine isnt running. Im assuming the problem is the plastic timing gear is shot to hell. When I tried to drop the engine, I decided to drop the whole k frame, however there was one bolt on the left hand side behind the suspension that just would not come out, even though the corresponding bolt on the other side came out fine. could there be a nut on this bolt? also, what is the easiest way to relive the tension put on the fron two sideways pins/bolt to get them out so I can finally drop this engine? Any other tips anyone has would be GREATLY appreciated, as I have no experience with mid engine car types||||reg||1
Z||000001||151 in. of love||02-06-2001||02:32 PM||||To relieve the tension on the front two bolts put a jack underneath the whole assembly or have cherry picker above the car pulling the engine/trans/frame up.<P>The bolt that is not comming out has a nut spot-welded to a plate on the inside of the frame. <BR>Sometimes it gets real corroded in there. <BR>Try a half inch breaker bar with a pipe on the end.<BR>If the weld inside breaks, (which it sometimes does) Then take a die-grinder and cut a small square out of the side of the frame (only about 1 in. wide and tall).<BR>Then you will be able to fit the end of a wrench on the nut inside.<BR>Keep posted on your success.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||02-06-2001||02:35 PM||||The nut might be spinning inside the frame, You need to lift up on the body to put the weight of the engine on the cradle. It should put enough pressure on the nut to stop it from turning. The front 2 bolts just need to be pulled out to drop the engine cradle assembly down.<P>Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||02-06-2001||08:28 PM||||Once you get inside the engine you will find the gears are not plastic.<BR>Have you done any trouble shooting to find the problem? You might be wasting your time and money with an unnecessary teardown.||||reg||1
